{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788975101,"nonce":"kpHCNphumRoRQNvZeRB4Ts8BATk=","title":"dev:analyze — the analysis god-hand the interact acceptance has to grind for","message":"`interact` (git-bug 70c1f9e) reaches `CompAnalyzable` through the player route, which is correct and is what the run needed. But the round trip is expensive: the pawn walks to the item, carries it to a research bench, and runs a wait toil of `ceil(Props.analysisDurationHours * 2500) / ResearchSpeed` ticks — ~1250 base per chip, plus two walks, plus a news halt on the completion letter. Three chips is three of those.\n\nThe game has a one-click escape and we do not: `CompAnalyzable.CompGetGizmosExtra` yields a `DEV: Finish analysis` Command_Action whose action is `OnAnalyzed(Find.CurrentMap.mapPawns.FreeColonistsSpawned.First())`, and `AnalysisManager.ForceCompleteAnalysisProgress(int id)` is public and does `AddAnalysisTask(id, 1)` on a miss then `value.timesDone = value.required`.\n\nThat is a `dev:*` verb, not a player one — the action-model rule is explicit that `dev:*` may bypass a gate and a player verb may not, so this does NOT belong inside `interact`.\n\nTwo shapes, and the difference matters:\n\n  * `OnAnalyzed(pawn)` runs the real completion — it increments, sends the\n    letter, and destroys the parent when `Props.destroyedOnAnalyzed`. That is\n    what the dev gizmo does.\n  * `ForceCompleteAnalysisProgress(id)` moves the LEDGER only: no letter, no\n    destroy, and it will register a task for an id that has none. Cheaper, and\n    the honest one for a fixture that only wants `research-set` unblocked.\n\nShip both under one verb with an explicit mode rather than picking one, because a fixture wants the second and a reproduction of the gizmo wants the first.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `dev:analyze {thing}` runs `CompAnalyzable.OnAnalyzed` with the named pawn (or\n  the gizmo's own `FreeColonistsSpawned.First()` when none is given), journals a\n  `dev` row with `cheat:true`, and reports the letter it sent and whether the\n  parent was destroyed.\n- `dev:analyze {thing, ledger_only:true}` calls\n  `AnalysisManager.ForceCompleteAnalysisProgress` instead and says in the reply\n  that no letter was sent and nothing was destroyed — the ledger moved and\n  nothing else did.\n- Either form refuses a thing with no `CompAnalyzable` by name.\n- The reply carries the same `analysis` block `interact-options` publishes\n  (`analysis_id`, `required`, `times_done\", `satisfied`, `research_unlocked`),\n  read AFTER the write, so the caller sees the ledger it just moved.\n- `research-set` on a project whose `requiredAnalyzed` names the def answers\n  `ok:true` immediately afterwards.\n- It is `dev:*` and it says so: no player verb gains an analysis bypass.","files":null}]}